  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 粒\ntitle: grain; small particle\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 11\nradical: 米\nradicalNumber: 119\nonyomi: [リュウ]\nkunyomi: [つぶ]\ndistractors: [位, 秒, 立]\n---\n\n# 粒 — grain; small particle\n\n**Strokes:** 11 · **Key (radical):** 米 (no. 119) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n粒 names a small grain, bead or drop and also counts small round objects. It identifies an individual unit or its shape, not one particular material.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** See 米 on the left and 立 on the right; picture one grain standing apart from the rest. This is an invented modern-shape memory aid.\n\nThe canonical key 米, no. 119, appears on the left.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| リュウ | on | 粒子 りゅうし - particle |\n| つぶ | kun | [粒](../words/粒.md) つぶ - grain; bead; drop |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [粒](../words/粒.md) つぶ - grain; bead; drop\n- 粒子 りゅうし - particle\n- 一粒 ひとつぶ - one grain; one bead; one drop\n\n## Notes\n\n- 一粒 ひとつぶ provides a usable native count. The dictionary also attests a リュウ counter reading; the リュウ row uses the unambiguous compound 粒子 instead of presenting the noun つぶ as freely pronounced りゅう.\n- Compare [粉](粉.md), powder, with a single 粒. Finely divided material and an individual grain are related ideas, not a rule that each visible particle is called flour.\n- [立](立.md), stand/set up, lacks 米. [位](位.md), rank/position, has a person-shaped left side rather than 米.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1167280, 1240530, 1287280, 1371880, 1508750, 1552890, 1552910.\n",
